      "title": "Note",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# TEST: EPS Distributor - one TEXT, three branches, each on/off (v0.75.0)\n\n**Just press Run.** No checkpoint, no lora, no GPU, no setup - it only moves\none string around. Takes a second.\n\nThe Distributor is no longer image-only: it carries **an image OR a text,\none type per node**. Its input starts as `any` and became `text` here the\nmoment the Text (Multiline) node was wired in - look at the input label and\nthe coloured wires: every socket on the node is STRING now.\n\n## Pass 1 - everything on (how it ships)\n\nPress **Run** once with all three toggles ON. All three **Preview as Text**\nnodes should show the same sentence. Three branches off ONE text in ONE run.\n\n## Pass 2 - turn a branch off (the actual test)\n\nClick the little **checkbox next to `out_2`** on the Distributor so it goes\ndark, press **Run** again: Branch A and C refresh, **Branch B stays blank**\n(its preview does not run at all - the branch is skipped, not fed an empty\nstring). Turn it back on and it returns.\n\n## Pass 3 - one type per node\n\nDrag a **Load Image**'s IMAGE output onto the Distributor's input: the wire\nis refused (the input is `text` now). Drag a checkpoint's MODEL onto it:\nrefused too, with a short message - images and text only, for now.\nDisconnect every wire and the input reads `any` again.\n\n## Where text Distributors earn their keep\n\nOne prompt from an **EPS Prompt Notebook** (or one `text` from an **EPS Run\nMultiplier**) fanned into several CLIP Text Encodes / save-path builders, with\nbranches you can switch off without rewiring.\n"
      ]
    }
